    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0391" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/925: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-03T13:00:00-03:30">January 3, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. My telegram number 56, December 10, noon.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d274-f1"/> The
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs today informed me that in view of the Paraguayan
                    Government’s continued refusal to accept the Uruguayan formula for carrying out
                    the terms of the Washington protocol,<anchor n="30" xml:id="d274-f2"/> which has
                    been accepted by Bolivia, the Bolivian Government recently declared that it
                    would break off negotiations here. Uruguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs has
                    requested the Bolivian Government to postpone such action for a couple of weeks
                    in order that an attempt might be made to induce Paraguay to accept the
                    formula.</p>
                <p>Uruguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs is sending Sampognaro, Uruguayan member of
                    the Brazilian-Uruguayan boundary commission, to Asunción tomorrow on a special
                    mission. He is to urge Paraguayan Minister for Foreign [Affairs?] to cooperate
                    in preventing break-down of the negotiations which would mean the collapse of
                    all the work accomplished at Washington.</p>
                <p>In this connection the Minister for Foreign Affairs expressed the hope that the
                    Government of the United States would make similar representations to
                    Paraguay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
